Adapted code: client/macos/Sources/GitGraphLayout.swift

Changes from Xit: the layout is a pure function of newest-first
(hash, parent hashes) already returned by `oberth git graph`. It does
not use libgit2, a repository, locks, or incremental batches. A commit
that no connection touches still receives a dot in the next free column
so every returned commit stays visible. GitGraphColumn.swift draws those
lane indexes with its own curves; it does not copy Xit's polyline.
